  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/41bef861-efa1-45a7-86c6-cb193703a900-9894755_S.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 194px;\" /></p><p>Magnetic field&nbsp;in plane of coil is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>The direction of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;component of magnetic field&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></math> is opposite of each other in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>z</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></math> positions.</p><p>So, the variation of magnetic field is shown below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f0cdb258-93c3-483a-8abc-f32cd35d83ab-9894755_C.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 154px;\" /></p>",
